  "claim_type": "correctness_fix_not_accuracy_improvement",
  "headline": "The bounce anchor is no more accurate than it was. The uncertainty it reports was wrong in three ways and is now materially less wrong; the reported sigma is LARGER, i.e. it claims LESS confidence than before, which is the correct outcome.",
  "defect": {
    "optimistic_on_depth": "measured RMS 1.65-2.97x the reported sigma; 29-47% coverage vs 68.3%",
    "conservative_in_image_plane": "0.36-0.88x; 78-97% coverage",
    "biased": "+0.068 to +0.124 m systematically away from the camera; a zero-mean sigma cannot express this",
    "consumed_isotropically": "ball_arc_solver.py:2357 divided all three world components by one scalar",
    "omitted_calibration_floor": "measured 0.101 m outdoor / 0.127 m wolverine / 0.232 m indoor",
    "non_radius_agnostic": "_ray_plane_pixel_sigma was called with the module constant BALL_RADIUS_M, not the caller's ball_radius_m"
  },
