  "residual_limitations": [
    "The bias term needs a per-sport bounce vertical-speed prior. It is the one input the model cannot derive, and it scales the bias linearly. TT3D's measured 1.94 m/s vs the pickleball default 4.0 m/s changes the modelled bias by ~2x.",
    "sigma_perp assumes an UNKNOWN ball heading, so it splits the sub-frame horizontal travel isotropically in the plane. In the TT3D back view the ball flies along the camera axis and has almost no cross-track motion, so sigma_perp is over-stated there by ~2.5x (image RMS ratio 0.40-0.44). Modelling heading would need the ball velocity, which the uncertainty function is not given.",
    "The ray-frame covariance is assumed DIAGONAL. Any real along/across correlation is unmodelled.",
    "The calibration residual floor could not be exercised by TT3D at all: TT3D's calibration is synthetic and exact (mapping reproduces its own pixels to 5.4e-13 px), so the floor term was 0 there. It is evidenced only by our own clips' measured floors and by the outdoor label set.",
    "Bias correction of the anchor POSITION is off by default. In that default posture the depth RMS ratio is 1.30-1.69 and coverage 0.46-0.57 -- better than the 1.65-2.97 / 0.29-0.47 before, but the bias still dominates until a consumer acts on it.",
    "External validation is table tennis. VERIFIED=0 for pickleball."
  ],
